From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rime-fork <rime-fork@localhost>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 08:47:25 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Long press a digit or punctuation key for its Shift symbol
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

sable/PenglaiLongPress.swift: in Penglai Zhuyin the number row and , . / ; - are zhuyin or tones; holding one past the key repeat delay types the key's Shift symbol instead (。 ？ ： ！ ...), as Shift+key would, with the schema's punctuation menus. The key's own press goes to librime as before and starts a timer; when it fires, if the window server saw no key released and no other key pressed since, and the input is still just that key added, put back the input from before it (digit keys commit the composition first, since Shift+digit selects a candidate) and send the Shift symbol. An auto-repeat of the key, if the client sends one, fires it too; later repeats are dropped. Many clients send no auto-repeats while press-and-hold is on, so the repeats alone are not enough. If the client committed the composition in the meantime and it was just that key (T3 opens its slash-command menu on a "/" at the start and commits it), take the key's character back out from before the caret first. Each step is logged (subsystem im.penglai.sable, category longpress; keys and steps only). Setting: long_press_symbols in sable.yaml (on unless false). This adds the file to the Xcode project and hooks it into the input controller.
---
 Squirrel.xcodeproj/project.pbxproj    |  4 ++
 sources/SquirrelInputController.swift | 74 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 78 insertions(+)

